    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136-a11">

                <pb facs="0309" n="213" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg213"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in 8 in No.
                    9—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Otin to the
                            Yamun.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-10-14"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 14,
                        1873</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">To His Highness Prince Kung and the
                        Ministers of the Yamun:</hi></p>
                <p>I have had the honor to receive the dispatch of yesterday’s date from your
                    highness, &amp;c., and have carefully examined it.</p>
                <p>In it you say that the articles which I submitted to you are totally
                        unlike<anchor n="*" xml:id="d136-f1"/> the points which were generally
                    agreed upon at the Russian legation on the 1st August. I can, therefore,
                    henceforth have no further transactions of a public nature with the Yamun; and
                    have accordingly requested the dean of the diplomatic body to attend to all
                    Spanish affairs on my behalf. I shall remain in Peking only on my private
                    affairs until I start on my journey, and have to request that I may henceforth
                    be regarded by the Yamun as only a private individual, in which position, if I
                    have any business, I shall ask the good offices of the clean of the diplomatic
                    body to attend to it.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>F. OTIN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d136-f1" n="*" xml:id="d136-f1-content">
                <p>The expression in the Chinese text for this discrepancy is far stronger than in
                    the preceding dispatch from the Chinese authorities, almost equivalent to a
                    declaration of antagonism; while theirs was disagreement, like the two parts of
                    a check.—<hi rendition="#small-caps">Note by</hi> S. W. W.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
